# graphify already merges this dir's .gitignore (gitignore semantics, last-match
# wins), so build artifacts and caches are excluded WITHOUT being repeated here:
# .venv/, build/, dist/, *.egg-info/, *.so, *.py[codz], __pycache__/, wheels/,
# the *_cache dirs, saved-models/, data/, .ophir/, graphify-out/, .claude/worktrees/.
# Only list things that are tracked / not gitignored but still don't belong in
# the knowledge map.

# SDD task ledger — per-task process briefs/reports. Useful as a work log,
# but they flood the graph with task-N nodes that crowd out the real
# architecture. Excluded from the knowledge map.
.superpowers/

# Lock files — pinned-dependency manifests, not source. graphify's built-in
# skip-list covers package-lock.json / Cargo.lock / poetry.lock / go.sum etc.
# but omits uv.lock (a ~1 MB churn file), so exclude the whole class explicitly.
*.lock

# Tooling / harness config — not part of the ophir package. graphify would
# otherwise ingest these (.json as code, .yaml as a document).
.vscode/
.claude/settings.json
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Project docs that are churn/meta rather than architecture: CHANGELOG.md is a
# high-churn release log, CLAUDE.md is agent operating guidance — neither
# describes the codebase structure the graph is meant to map.
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
